# Blocks the gates could not judge, which someone checked another way.
#
# G2 marks a block `not-evaluated` when Trivy has no check for its kind (a
# Rollout, a PyTorchJob, a List), or returned nothing for the file. G3 marks a
# block `missing-crd` when the cluster lacks its custom resource definition.
# Neither is a pass. If such a block holds a pod template, the gate exits 1
# unless the block is listed here, because the pod template went unread.
#
# One entry per line:
#
#     chapter | what | reason
#
# chapter  the path under full-guide/, for example 05-security/02-pod-security.md
# what     what the gate printed for the block: a kind such as Rollout, or
#          no-scanner-result. A block with several is allowed only when all
#          of them are listed. `*` allows every one in that chapter.
# reason   how the block was checked instead, for example "rendered with
#          the chart and run through Trivy in the pull request". Required.
#
# The pull request that adds a line must also say how the block was checked.
# Remove the line when the chapter stops needing it.
15-day-to-day-production-ops/06-progressive-delivery-in-production.md | Rollout | Checked by hand against the 01.01 baseline, and by jsonschema against the rollouts.argoproj.io CRD of argo-rollouts chart 2.43.8 (app v1.10.1), extracted with helm template. sf-pilot has no Argo Rollouts CRD, so the server dry-run cannot run there.
14-eks-in-production-a-to-z/16-developer-experience-for-k8s-teams.md | Config | skaffold.yaml is a Skaffold build config that only the skaffold CLI reads. Its manifests entry lists the 2.2 block, which the static and admission gates check. Its keys follow the Skaffold v4beta14 schema (manifests.rawYaml, deploy.kubectl), checked against the upstream config.go; skaffold itself was not run.
full-guide/examples/bookstore-platform/ml/training-workflow.yaml | WorkflowTemplate | each of the four templates was rendered to a Pod (template securityContext, volumes and container, token setting from the workflow spec) and scanned with Trivy: no core check (KSV-0012, KSV-0014, KSV-0001, KSV-0003, KSV-0030) fails; KSV-0011 (no CPU limit, by baseline 01.03), KSV-0036 (token mounted for the Argo executor, dedicated ServiceAccount) and KSV-0125 are reported and accepted; transcript evidence/13-08.txt, section 4
full-guide/examples/bookstore-platform/observability/otel-collector.yaml | OpenTelemetryCollector | The operator renders this CR into a DaemonSet from its securityContext and podSecurityContext, which set the restricted fields. The CR was checked against the v1beta1 CRD schema of chart 0.115.0 (no unknown fields, no schema errors) and its config passed otelcol-contrib validate in the pinned image (13.09 transcript). The operator-rendered pods were not dry-run, because the CRD is not installed in the lab.
full-guide/examples/bookstore-platform/search/debezium-connector.yaml | KafkaConnect | Strimzi 0.40.0 CR with no Trivy check. Its pod template was checked by hand against the chart's CRD schema (helm pull strimzi-kafka-operator 0.40.0): connectContainer and pod securityContext are set, and each plugin artifact carries a sha512sum.
full-guide/examples/bookstore-platform/search/debezium-connector.yaml | KafkaUser | Strimzi 0.40.0 CR with no Trivy check and no pod template. Its fields were checked against the chart's CRD schema (helm pull strimzi-kafka-operator 0.40.0), with no unknown fields.
full-guide/examples/bookstore-platform/search/debezium-connector.yaml | KafkaConnector | Strimzi 0.40.0 CR with no Trivy check and no pod template. Its fields were checked against the chart's CRD schema (helm pull strimzi-kafka-operator 0.40.0), with no unknown fields.
